This is a small shopping-list app (front-end + perl CGI back-end).

History
- Started in Sep-2025 as a lightweight alternative to cloud services.
- Since the initial version the app gained journal support, entry-sorting for journal lists, autosave and improved touch/drag handling.
- Jan-2026: Added photo support with dedicated photo.cgi backend and photo.js module.

Overview
- Front-end: JS app for browser, desktop webview or mobile.
- Back-end: perl CGI (api.cgi / index.cgi / photo.cgi) serving JSON lists, photos, and static assets.

HTTP interface
- GET  .../shopping/                      - list available JSON files.
- GET  .../shopping/api.cgi/shop?l=NAME  - return the JSON for list NAME.
- POST .../shopping/api.cgi/shop?l=NAME  - create or update the JSON for list NAME.
- POST .../shopping/photo.cgi/upload     - upload a photo (multipart/form-data), returns JSON with filename.
- GET  .../shopping/photo.cgi/<user>/<filename> - serve an uploaded photo.
- Static files (index.html, shopping.js, CSS, images) are served by the back-end.

Data format (canonical example)
- The JSON is intentionally simple. Lists may include a journal flag; there are no per-section IDs or per-item metadata fields in the current implementation.

{
  "name": "shop",
  "type": "journal",  // "journal" for date-based lists, omit for regular shopping lists
  "items": [
    { "type": "section", "title": "Meats", "collapsed": false, "items": [
      { "type": "item", "text": "Bacon", "checked": false },
      { "type": "item", "text": "Steak", "checked": true }
    ]},
    { "type": "section", "title": "Vegetables", "collapsed": true, "items": [
      { "type": "item", "text": "Carrots", "checked": true },
      { "type": "text", "text": "Remember to check the special offers" },
      { "type": "photo", "filename": "IMG_20260105_123456.jpg", "created": "2026-01-05T12:34:56Z" }
    ]}
  ]
}

There will be more fields later, for example dates when created and modified.

Item types
- Lines can be created by typing a single character prefix followed by Enter:
  - 'x' or 'o' - checkbox item (checked or unchecked)
  - '.' - plain text line (no checkbox)
  - 's ' - section header (converts current line to section)
  - 'p' - photo (triggers file picker/camera, uploads photo)

Journals
- Create a journal-type list via the main menu ("New Journal").
- Journal lists automatically organize items into date-based sections (YYYY-MM-DD format).
- Section titles show day of week, and journal entries can be sorted chronologically.
- Use "New entry for date..." menu item to create entries for specific dates.
- Toggle a regular list to/from journal type via the main menu ("Toggle Journal").

Photos
- Type 'p' and press Enter on any line to add a photo.
- Photos are uploaded to photo/<user>/ on the server.
- Photo items are stored in JSON with filename and created timestamp.
- Photos display inline, constrained to fit the container (max-width: 100%, max-height: 90vh).
- Click on a photo to open the full-size version in a new tab.
- Photos are served via photo.cgi with authentication (REMOTE_USER must match).


The UI consists of a top line with the name of the list we are working with,
and a pull-down menu with options to add a new list, delete this one, and the
same operations as in a section menu.

The main body of the UI consists of (nested) sections that contains lines. Most
have a checkbox on them, some can be plain text. Each section head will have
a pulldown menu with options for (un)checking all items in it,  for adding new
items, for filtering the display to show only checked or unchecked items, etc.

The item lines have (a optional) checkbox, some text, and a pulldown menu with
options for deleting the item, adding a new one, or duplicating this one.

Clicking on any text (section title or item text) allows editing it.

After inserting a new item, the UI continues to insert a new one, unless the
text is empty.

Any changes made in the UI should be autosaved to back-end after a few seconds.


At the moment the drag.sj will only work on my desktop. I have tried to make it
work on the mobile but chaggpt always fucks up the touch handling, so the
system gets confused which gestures are for the app and which for the browser
itself. F.ex. dragging down will want to refresh the page, no matter what.

There is an example apache config under etc, adjust as needed.
